+This will end the request with `400 - Bad Request` status code and a [Problem Details (RFC 9457)](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457) response (`Content-Type: application/problem+json`):
 
 ```json
 {
   "date": "2025-06-05T04:20:00.0Z",
-  "status": 400,
   "statusText": "Bad Request",
   "message": "Invalid user input",
   "data": {
     "field": "email"
-  }
+  },
+  "type": "about:blank",
+  "title": "Bad Request",
+  "status": 400,
+  "detail": "Invalid user input"
 }
 ```
 
+`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail` and `instance` are the standard members. `statusText`, `message`, `data`, `unhandled` and the `body` properties are kept as extension members. `title` defaults to the standard phrase of the status code (omitted for unknown statuses), `type` defaults to `about:blank`, and `instance` is only included when set. `body` keys never override the standard members.
+
 ### `HTTPError` Fields
 
 - `status`: HTTP status code in the range 200–599.
